---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
const EMAIL = 'tsouth2@gmail.com';
---
<Legal
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy | Family Bakery: Merge & Bake"
  heading="Family Bakery privacy"
  description="What Family Bakery: Merge & Bake keeps, what it sends, and what it never does."
  lastUpdated="October 10, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Family Bakery: Merge &amp; Bake is a merge game for Android and iPhone. It has no accounts, no ads
    and no tracking. It shares a few anonymous usage counts, which you can turn off. This policy covers
    the game only.
  </p>

  <h2>Your café stays on your phone</h2>
  <p>
    Your progress, settings and café are saved on your device. We don't upload them anywhere. If your phone
    backs up apps to your Google or Apple account, that backup includes your café, so it can come back after a
    reinstall; Google and Apple handle those backups under your account. If you use Move my café in Settings,
    the café code is created on your phone and goes only where you paste it.
  </p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    The game sells one optional purchase that opens the whole café. Payment is handled by Google Play or
    the App Store; we never see your card or payment details. To confirm and restore the purchase, the game uses
    <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat</a>, which receives a random ID created by the app,
    your purchase records and basic technical details such as app version, device type and country. We use
    this only to unlock the game for you.
  </p>

  <h2>Anonymous usage counts</h2>
  <p>
    To see which parts of the game people enjoy and where they get stuck, the game sends a few counts to
    <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">PostHog</a>, our analytics provider in the United States: when the
    game opens, which day and chapter you're on, finished days and chapters, Cake Sort wins and losses, goals
    claimed, energy refills, when the unlock screen appears, purchases and restores, and whether reminders were
    allowed, along with the app version and whether it's Android or iPhone. Each launch uses a new random number
    that is never saved, so the counts aren't linked to you or to each other across launches. They never include
    your name, your café or save, or any device or advertising ID. PostHog receives your IP address when the
    counts arrive, as any website would; the game asks it not to work out your location. Turn this off anytime
    with Share anonymous usage in Settings.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell or share your information, show ads, track you across apps or websites, or ask for your
    name, email, contacts, location, photos or microphone.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The game is meant for players 13 and over and does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Uninstalling the game deletes your café from the device. Usage counts can't be traced back to a player,
    so there is nothing of yours in them to delete. To delete the purchase records held by RevenueCat, email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. Your store account keeps its own purchase history.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date above changes with it. Questions can be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
